WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.200
Even with all the publicity she's received
since Game of Thrones premiered, there are

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.640
still plenty of fun facts and discoveries
to be made about the talented actress Emilia

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.600
Clarke, a singular talent who still has an
extraordinary future ahead of her. Here are

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.080
just a few of the untold truths about Clarke's
life and career.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.511
Thanks to her starring role in HBO's massive
hit series Game of Thrones, Emilia Clarke

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.180
has become one of the most recognizable faces
on television.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.930
Beyond Game of Thrones, Clarke has appeared
in other high-profile roles too, including

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:33.920
star turns in films like Solo: A Star Wars
Story and Terminator Genisys. So far, her

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.629
most significant role has certainly been Daenerys
Targaryen, otherwise known as Khaleesi and

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:39.820
the Mother of Dragons.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.900
Game of Thrones is a notoriously fleshy adventure
series, and Emilia Clarke racked up quite

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:51.129
a few nude scenes during the show's first
season. In 2017, she told Actors on Actors:

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:58.090
"The naked stuff is always difficult… it's
always kind of hard because it's just… uncomfortable

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.429
for many, many, many, many reasons."

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:04.500
As she told Entertainment Weekly, her life
took a turn for the incredibly awkward when

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.480
she wound up watching one of those nude scenes
with her family. Whoops.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.500
"I ended up sitting them down and being like,
‘Let’s watch it’ — and then instantly

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.110
regretting it. … My dad was like, ‘Again?'”

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.740
Graham Norton was clearly tickled by that
anecdote:

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.300
"Did you watch it with your parents?"

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:19.860
"Yes."

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.040
Clarke also had no qualms about appearing
nude on stage in a production of Breakfast

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:32.049
at Tiffany's, which premiered at New York's
Cort Theater in 2013. Naturally, a big name

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:37.340
like Clarke drew huge crowds, including some
exceedingly creepy patrons who took photos

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.080
of Clarke during her nude scenes.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:44.500
Unfortunately, the show was slammed by critics
and closed after only 38 performances. It's

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:49.479
too bad her first theatrical outing was tarnished
by weird audience members and bad reviews...

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:52.990
but at least now she has a Broadway credit
to her name, and there will likely be many

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.000
more in the future.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.680
After her breakout role on Game of Thrones,
Clarke was inundated with film offers, with

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.330
one big franchise standing out from the pack.
Reportedly, Clarke was offered the lead role

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:09.530
of Anastasia Steele in Fifty Shades of Grey,
the first in a trilogy of theoretically sexy

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.740
films based on the bestselling series of trashy
novels.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.530
Ultimately, Clarke decided to turn down the
role, which famously went to Dakota Johnson,

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.750
who starred alongside British actor Jamie
Dornan for the entirety of the series.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.660
In a 2015 interview with Kiss FM, Clarke played
a little bit coy about the decision:

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.600
"Is it true that you turned down the Fifty
Shades of Grey role?"

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.120
"Ooooh… well! Uhhhhh… ay-juh… Yeah."

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.640
Clarke has explained why she made that decision.
Fifty Shades could have certainly given her

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.190
more exposure as an actor, but it wasn't the
kind of exposure she wanted. After her history

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:47.460
of nude scenes on stage and screen, Clarke
didn't want to be labeled as any specific

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.180
type of performer. She says she really doesn't
regret turning down the role. Considering

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.300
the bleak critical reception the trilogy received,
it seems like she definitely made the right

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.040
choice.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.040
Add Emilia Clarke's name to the long, illustrious
list of tattooed celebrities. Clarke's first

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.560
tattoo was dedicated to her role in Me Before
You, where she played a big-hearted caretaker

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.960
who has a tattoo of a bumblebee. Well, guess
what Clarke got inked on her pinky finger?

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.180
"I got a bumblebee."

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.280
"And what is that?"

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.140
"It's so badass. Badass girl, you got a tattoo,
what'd you get? A bumblebee. There's still

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:20.720
plaster on it."

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.060
Naturally, Clarke needed to get a Game of
Thrones tattoo, too. And guess what she went

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.070
for this time?

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.043
"I was in a tattoo parlor the other day trying
to make an appointment, and they said they

00:03:29.043 --> 00:03:32.980
were full because you're coming in to get
a tattoo of a dragon?"

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.480
"Yes."

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.540
Maybe they aren't the biggest dragons we've
ever seen. But they are dragons.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.340
Clarke was seemingly born to be an actor,
considering that her father worked in the

00:03:42.341 --> 00:03:46.780
theater community in London as a sound engineer.
The first show Clarke ever saw as a child

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.450
was Showboat. She was enthralled, falling
in love with the theater right then and there.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:56.290
However, her dad wasn't quite so enthusiastic
about her goals. In fact, he took her to a

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:00.290
real audition in the West End in the hopes
of scaring her away from the profession. She

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:04.380
bombed completely, showing up unprepared with
just a folk song to her name.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.500
As she continued pursuing her dream, Clarke
said her dad's only advice was to be aware

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.660
of the many pitfalls of the profession. He
reminded her that actors rarely make a living

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.850
off their passion and even told her that the
only line she ever needed to memorize was:

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.100
"Do you want fries with that?"

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.500
We're sure her dad had the best intentions,
but fans around the world must be glad Clarke

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.700
kept at it. She eventually attended the prestigious
Drama Centre London, and the rest is history.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.020
Well, more or less...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.960
After graduating, Clarke's acting career got
off to a rather quiet start. She had a few

00:04:34.971 --> 00:04:40.000
bit parts in commercials and made appearances
on British shows like Doctors and even a dreadful

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.880
SyFy original movie called Triassic Attack.
In 2010, Screen International named her one

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.400
of the "UK Stars of Tomorrow," and they were
right on the money: She scored her audition

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.180
for Game of Thrones shortly after that career
milestone.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:56.700
But Clarke still had to make sure her bills
were paid. At the time she landed the role,

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:01.040
Clarke was reportedly working six jobs, including
a gig as a real estate agent.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.200
Due to the importance of that particular audition,
Clarke called in sick to her catering job

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.640
that day. Obviously her efforts were well
worth it, as she booked the role of a lifetime

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:14.010
and quickly became one of the most celebrated
young actresses in the industry. Take that,

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.010
catering job.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:20.780
The fact that Clarke even got to audition
for Game of Thrones is rather extraordinary,

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:24.810
considering the pilot had already been shot
by the time she got that fateful call from

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:28.930
her agent. However, the original pilot was
a dismal failure. Before you think that's

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:34.110
too harsh a description, it comes from series
creators David Benioff Benioff and D.B. Weiss,

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:38.889
who blamed unclear storytelling, melodramatic
death scenes, and bad casting. They eventually

00:05:38.889 --> 00:05:41.300
reshot about ninety percent of the episode.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:45.840
The creators have politely declined to discuss
why they recast the role of Daenerys, which

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.310
was originally played by actress Tamzin Merchant,
best known for roles like Catherine Howard

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.810
on The Tudors. The original pilot never saw
the light of day, and now it's impossible

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.400
to imagine anyone but Clarke playing Daenerys.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.600
Over the course of seven seasons, she's been
nominated for several Emmy awards and has

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.990
made the role completely her own. She'll probably
be referred to as the "Mother of Dragons"

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.520
for many more years to come.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.180
Emilia Clarke is the first to admit that her
Game of Thrones audition took an odd turn.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:18.200
Prior to her audition, she'd spent hours scouring
Wikipedia to learn more about A Song of Ice

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:22.360
and Fire, George R. R. Martin's book series
on which Game of Thrones is based.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:27.240
As she told Jimmy Fallon, showrunners Benioff
and Weiss asked Clarke about her other talents

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.280
after she read a few lines of dialogue. Then
they suggested that she do a dance.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:36.420
"I just… I don't know how to do it, but
I did the Funky Chicken. And it kind of morphed

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.680
into The Robot… And I sort of heard, I heard
some laughter going on…"

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:44.300
Afterwards, she evidently didn't feel particularly
hopeful about the audition. Of course, she

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.420
was cast in the role shortly afterwards.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.920
Clarke may have gotten giggles out of the
showrunners, but they still got a taste of

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.170
the remarkable intensity she uses to bring
Daenerys to life. In fact, it sounds like

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.810
they were completely sold on her right out
of the gate.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:00.540
"Our certitude was as religious as Daenerys's:
She was the one."

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:06.380
Until recently, Emilia Clarke kept one period
of her life completely private. In a moving

00:07:06.389 --> 00:07:11.650
personal essay published in The New Yorker
in March 2019, she revealed that she'd survived

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:15.900
a very serious health scare. During a session
with her personal trainer, Clarke suffered

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.500
a debilitating brain aneurysm. Only a third
of patients survive what she endured.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:25.340
After a minimally invasive form of brain surgery,
Clarke learned that she had a smaller aneurysm

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:30.090
elsewhere in her brain that could also pop.
Shaky, exhausted, and partially reliant on

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:35.320
morphine, Clarke bravely went back to work
and continued filming Game of Thrones. Then,

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:40.180
in 2013, the second aneurysm burst, requiring
a much more invasive surgery. An incredibly

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.310
difficult road to recovery lay ahead.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:48.160
"The second one, a bit of my brain actually
died. If a part of your brain doesn't get

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.680
blood to it for a minute, it will just no
longer work."

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.780
In her essay, Clarke writes that she's now,
quote, "one hundred percent" recovered. She

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.520
also started a charity called SameYou to help
patients suffering from strokes and other

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:04.770
brain injuries. As a professional actress
and public figure, Clarke's brave decision

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.240
to speak out about the most difficult period
of her life speaks volumes about her character.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:15.600
Despite her personal successes, 2016 was a
difficult year for the young star. In the

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:20.320
aftermath of Brexit, an issue near and dear
to Clarke's heart as a Londoner, she lost

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:25.100
a family member shortly after the vote, and
both situations set her adrift personally

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:25.880
and professionally.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:30.540
Clarke's father had suffered from cancer for
years and succumbed to his illness in July

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:35.999
2016. Sadly, she couldn't be there during
his final days. While his health declined,

00:08:35.999 --> 00:08:39.990
she was filming a movie in Kentucky. After
cutting the filming short, she finally arrived

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:44.779
in London only to learn that he'd already
passed away. This was absolutely devastating

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:49.320
to Clarke, especially since she was due back
on the Game of Thrones set in three weeks.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:53.820
She told Rolling Stone that the experience
only made her stronger. Since her father's

00:08:53.829 --> 00:08:57.319
death, she's praised the nurses who cared
for him, vowing that she'd always support

00:08:57.319 --> 00:09:01.839
England's medical community from that day
forward. In 2018, she became an ambassador

00:09:01.839 --> 00:09:06.350
for London's Royal College of Nursing, joining
in the school's ongoing campaign for financial

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.860
support from the British government and the
NHS.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:14.360
When a cast is sworn to secrecy while filming
one of the world's hottest shows in far-flung

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:19.880
locations, it's only natural that they'd become
close friends. Clarke is no exception. Daenerys

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:24.329
started off the series with a wedding to Khal
Drogo, played by future Aquaman star Jason

00:09:24.329 --> 00:09:28.140
Momoa. The two became fast friends while they
were quartered in Morocco together.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:32.600
Though Drogo was dead by the end of the first
season, Momoa and Clarke have remained very

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:37.160
close. In fact, they refer to each other as,
quote, "the moon of my life" and "my sun and

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:41.190
stars." To this day, Momoa seems like one
of Clarke's biggest supporters, and fans are

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:45.250
always delighted by their reunions, which
have taken place at major award shows and

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:50.400
Comic-Con, where Momoa made a surprise appearance
that did indeed succeed in startling Clarke.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:55.110
Now, as the show ends, Clarke will almost
certainly be closing out her character's storyline

00:09:55.110 --> 00:10:00.070
alongside Kit Harington. He of course plays
the brooding Jon Snow, the presumed bastard

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:05.220
who is actually Daenerys' royal nephew and
her new lover. Yup. Luckily, she and Harington

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:08.870
seem to be having a great time together on
set, especially when they're joking around

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.100
about their love scenes.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:13.379
"I mean I think 'ughhh' might be the reaction."

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.340
"I like looking at her and going 'Ugh, god,
I'm sorry.'"

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.300
The pair have been friends since the first
season, and each of them is excited to finish

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.300
the series with a friend at their side.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:28.140
As Daenerys, Clarke is no stranger to traveling
through foreign lands, often on foot. At the

00:10:28.149 --> 00:10:32.389
beginning of Game of Thrones, she begins a
long journey from the native land of the Dothraki

00:10:32.389 --> 00:10:37.259
warrior clan, located across the Narrow Sea
from Westeros, in order to finally take back

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.360
the Iron Throne of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:43.740
She gets turned around several times over,
ending up in Slaver's Bay and subsequently

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:48.370
taking control of several slave cities before
finally ending up in Westeros in the seventh

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:52.779
season. Thanks to this storyline, Clarke herself
has gotten to travel to several exotic filming

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:57.160
locations over the years, including Croatia,
Ireland, Iceland, and Spain.

00:10:57.449 --> 00:11:02.500
Like her character, Clarke became a world
traveler at a young age. At just 16, she embarked

00:11:02.509 --> 00:11:07.040
on a backpacking trip through Northern India,
continuing into Tibet, having made the journey

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:11.140
to scatter the ashes of her grandmother, who
was born in Delhi. A few years later, she

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:15.350
made a similar journey through Southeast Asia
as well as South Africa, proving that she's

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:19.100
just as adventurous as her signature character.
No surprise there!

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.540
Check out one of our newest videos right here!
Plus, even more Looper videos about Game of

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:27.369
Thrones are coming soon. Subscribe to our
YouTube channel and hit the bell so you don't

00:11:27.369 --> 00:11:28.329
miss a single one.

